; Document order: the cross-pass reference inside the first pass, then
; the unscoped one at root. Both land on the reference site's slot path,
; which is where the author has to make the change — and the paths
; differ only by the enclosing `pass`, which is the scope that made the
; first one a miss and the second one unscoped.
(diagnostics
  (diagnostic :code not_cross_ref :path [pass bind uniform])
  (diagnostic :code cross_ref_outside_scope :path [bind uniform]))
